      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The paper describes 3 men aged 43, 62 and 66 years with left main coronary artery occlusion. In all patients well-developed collateral circulation from right to left coronary artery was present. They were operated in cardiopulmonary bypass and two bypass grafts were implanted in each of them. There were no deaths in the perioperative period. Actually all the patients are alive and have no angina."},
